            "post": {
                "tags": [
                    "Diagnosis"
                ],
                "summary": "Analyze medical description for possible disease diagnoses",
                "description": "Analyzes a patient's medical description and returns a ranked differential diagnosis list.  \nThis unified endpoint supports model selection through the optional `model` parameter.\n\n**Available Models:**\n- **`gpt56terra`**: current default model (best quality/speed/cost balance), with WebSocket progress.\n- **`gpt54mini`**: previous compact default (backward compatibility), with WebSocket progress.\n- **`gpt5`**: multimodal model (text + images), with WebSocket progress.\n- **`gpt5mini`**: legacy compact model (backward compatibility), with WebSocket progress.\n- **`gpt5nano`**: ultra-compact model, with WebSocket progress.\n- **`gpt4o`**: legacy fast model (backward compatibility).\n- **`o3`**: legacy alias. Internally resolved to `gpt56terra`.\n\n**Model Selection Guidelines:**\n- Use **`gpt56terra`** for current standard and high-volume cases.\n- Use **`gpt5`** when image understanding is required.\n- Keep **`gpt54mini`**, **`gpt5mini`**, **`gpt5nano`**, and **`gpt4o`** for legacy/compatibility scenarios.\n- Keep **`o3`** only while migrating older clients; it maps to Terra.\n\n**Deployment note:** In APIM-hosted environments the server currently resolves every requested model to `gpt56terra`. Model selection is honored only when the API runs locally (`NODE_ENV=local`).\n\n**Intent Routing:** Before diagnosis, the request is classified as:\n- **`go`**: patient case ready for differential diagnosis.\n- **`explain`**: the text is a medical question; the UI may suggest Ask.\n- **`enrich`**: more clinical context would improve the differential.\n\nThese actions suggest a path and never block diagnosis. Set `forceDiagnosis` to `true` when the user explicitly chooses to continue.\n\n**WebSocket Flow for Long-Running Models:**\nWhen using `gpt56terra`, `gpt54mini`, `gpt5`, `gpt5mini`, or `gpt5nano`:\n1. Call `/pubsub/negotiate` to establish WebSocket connection.\n2. Send diagnosis request to `/diagnose` with the selected model.\n3. Receive immediate HTTP response with `result: \"processing\"`.\n4. Monitor WebSocket for progress events.\n5. Receive final result via WebSocket.\n\nSet `response_mode` to `direct` to wait for a synchronous HTTP response instead of using WebSocket.\n\n**WebSocket Message Types:**\n- **Progress**: `{\"type\":\"progress\",\"step\":\"translation|ai_processing|anonymization|finalizing\",\"message\":\"...\",\"percentage\":10-95}`\n- **Result**: `{\"type\":\"result\",\"status\":\"success\",\"data\":{...}}` (same payload shape as HTTP final response)\n- **Error**: `{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"...\",\"code\":\"...\"}`\n\nFor best results:\n- Provide relevant patient details (age, sex, main symptoms, onset/evolution).\n- Include relevant personal/family medical history where available.\n- Recommended length: **200-2000** characters.\n\n**Detailed Response Format:** For each suggested diagnosis, the system returns:\n- **Diagnosis**: condition name\n- **Description**: brief clinical summary\n- **Symptoms in common**: symptoms matching the condition\n- **Symptoms not in common**: symptoms that do not typically match\n\nThis format supports safer differential reasoning by showing both matching and conflicting evidence.\n\nThe response also includes language detection, anonymization metadata, and intent-routing fields (`queryType`, `intentAction`, `intentReason`, optional `suggestedPage`).\n\n**Using `diseases_list` parameter:** If you provide diseases in `diseases_list`, the system excludes them and proposes alternatives. This is useful when:\n- Initial diagnoses were not accurate and you want to explore alternatives.\n- You want a wider differential diagnosis.\n- You want to focus on less common conditions.\n\nExample input with `diseases_list`:\n```json\n{\n  \"description\": \"13-month-old patient. First focal seizure at three months. Multiple tonic-clonic seizures. Febrile seizures. One status epilepticus at eight months.\",\n  \"diseases_list\": \"Dravet syndrome, Lennox-Gastaut syndrome, Febrile seizures Plus (FS+)\",\n  \"myuuid\": \"01dd5910-de38-48df-9840-091bc918c943\"\n}\n```\n\n**Supported Languages**: The description can be in any language supported by Azure AI Translator (see [supported languages](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/translator/language-support)). The response will be returned in the same language as the input description. If the optional parameter `lang` is not provided, the default language for responses will be English.\n\n**Anonymization**: The response includes anonymized versions of the patient description where personally identifiable information (PII) is replaced with [ANON-N] (where N is the character count), and then converted to asterisks in the final output. PII includes full names, addresses, contact details, Social Security Numbers, and any unique identification numbers. Importantly, age is NOT considered PII in this context and is preserved. All medical specifics (symptoms, diagnosis, treatment plans, and lab results) are maintained intact. The response provides both a text version with asterisks and an HTML-formatted version with blacked-out sections for visualization.\n\n**Queue System**: Requests may be queued during high traffic for any model. A queue status will be returned for tracking, including the selected processing region based on user timezone and model capacity.",
                "operationId": "post-diagnose",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "name": "X-Tenant-Id",
                        "in": "header",
                        "description": "Tenant identifier for multi-tenant data segmentation. Required for SaaS/hospital clients, optional for marketplace clients.\n",
