                "description": "Analyzes medical documents, images, and text to extract relevant clinical information and generate a comprehensive patient description, then continues into asynchronous diagnosis.\n\nThis unified endpoint processes various types of medical input:\n- **Documents**: PDF, DOC, DOCX, XLS, XLSX, TXT files containing medical records, lab results, or clinical notes\n- **Images**: JPG, PNG, TIFF, BMP, WEBP files of medical images, photos of documents, or visual symptoms\n- **Text**: Direct text input describing symptoms or medical history\n\nAt least one of `text`, `document`, or `image` is required. Every call creates a new upload; reuse it in `/diagnose` and `/disease/info` through the returned `uploadId`.\n\n**Processing Pipeline:**\n1. Extracts text from uploaded documents using OCR and document intelligence\n2. Classifies images as document-only, mixed, medical visual, or unknown\n3. Uses OCR-only for high-confidence document images, OCR plus vision for mixed images, and direct vision for medical, unknown, or failed routes\n4. Summarizes the combined text when it is longer than 1000 characters\n5. Starts diagnosis processing asynchronously with the current default model (`gpt56terra`)\n\n**Asynchronous Diagnosis Flow:**\n1. Call `/pubsub/negotiate` with the same `myuuid` to establish the WebSocket connection.\n2. Send the multimodal request to `/medical/analyze`.\n3. Receive an immediate HTTP response with `result: \"processing\"`, plus `description`, `uploadId`, `images`, `imageRouting`, `documents`, `isImageOnly`, `summarized`, `model`, and `correlationId`.\n4. Monitor WebSocket for progress events (`type: progress`, field `step`).\n5. Receive the final diagnosis via WebSocket (`type: result`), in the same payload shape as `/diagnose`.\n\n**File Limits:**\n- Maximum 5 documents per request\n- Maximum 5 images per request\n- Documents and images combined must not exceed 20 MB\n- Supported document formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX, XLS, XLSX, TXT\n- Supported image formats: JPG, PNG, TIFF, BMP, WEBP\n\n**Deployment note:** In APIM-hosted environments the server currently resolves every requested model to `gpt56terra`. Model selection is honored only when the API runs locally (`NODE_ENV=local`).\n\nThe `lang` parameter is optional - if not provided, the language will be automatically detected.\n",
