                "description": "Establishes a WebSocket connection for real-time updates during diagnosis, Ask, and multimodal processing.\n\nThis endpoint is used for long-running requests (`gpt56terra`, `gpt54mini`, `gpt5`, `gpt5mini`, `gpt5nano`, and the legacy `o3` alias). The typical workflow is:\n\n1. Call this endpoint with a unique user ID (`myuuid`)\n2. Receive a WebSocket URL and access token\n3. Connect to the WebSocket using the provided credentials\n4. Send your request to `/diagnose`, `/ask`, or `/medical/analyze` with the same `myuuid`\n5. Receive real-time updates through the WebSocket:\n   - Progress updates with current step and percentage\n   - Queue status if the request is queued\n   - Final result when processing completes\n   - Error notifications if processing fails\n\n**WebSocket Message Types:**\n- **Progress**: `{\"type\":\"progress\",\"step\":\"translation|ai_processing|anonymization|medical_question|finalizing\",\"message\":\"...\",\"percentage\":10-95}`\n- **Result**: `{\"type\":\"result\",\"status\":\"success\",\"data\":{...}}` (same payload shape as the HTTP final response)\n- **Error**: `{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"...\",\"code\":\"...\"}`\n- **Queued**: `{\"type\":\"queued\",\"status\":\"queued\",\"queueInfo\":{...}}`\n\nThe connection remains active until processing is complete or an error occurs.\nClients should implement reconnection logic in case of network interruptions.\n\n`myuuid` is required and must be a UUID. The returned `hubName` is `diagnose` for all of these flows.\n",
                "operationId": "post-pubsub-negotiate",
                "requestBody": {
