        "/ask": {
            "post": {
                "tags": [
                    "Medical Questions"
                ],
                "summary": "Answer general medical questions",
                "description": "Answers general medical questions with concise, evidence-based educational information.\n\nThis endpoint is the Ask companion to `/diagnose`. Use it when the user is asking about a condition, medication, test, or other medical topic rather than submitting a patient case for differential diagnosis.\n\n**Intent Routing:** Before answering, the request is classified as:\n- **`explain`**: medical question; the system returns an educational `medicalAnswer`.\n- **`go`**: the text looks like a patient case ready for differential diagnosis; the UI may suggest Diagnose.\n- **`enrich`**: more clinical context would improve a differential; the UI may suggest Diagnose.\n\nThese actions suggest a path and never block the user. A patient case submitted to Ask may still return a routing suggestion (`suggestedPage: \"home\"`) instead of forcing a diagnosis. To run differential diagnosis, call `/diagnose` (set `forceDiagnosis` to `true` when the user explicitly chooses to continue).\n\n**Available Models:**\n- **`gpt56terra`**: current default model (best quality/speed/cost balance), with WebSocket progress.\n- **`gpt54mini`**: previous compact default (backward compatibility), with WebSocket progress.\n- **`gpt5`**: multimodal model (text + images), with WebSocket progress.\n- **`gpt5mini`**: legacy compact model (backward compatibility), with WebSocket progress.\n- **`gpt5nano`**: ultra-compact model, with WebSocket progress.\n- **`gpt4o`**: legacy fast model (backward compatibility).\n- **`o3`**: legacy alias. Internally resolved to `gpt56terra`.\n\n**Deployment note:** In APIM-hosted environments the server currently resolves every requested model to `gpt56terra`. Model selection is honored only when the API runs locally (`NODE_ENV=local`).\n\n**WebSocket Flow for Long-Running Models:**\nWhen using `gpt56terra`, `gpt54mini`, `gpt5`, `gpt5mini`, or `gpt5nano`:\n1. Call `/pubsub/negotiate` to establish WebSocket connection.\n2. Send the question to `/ask` with the selected model.\n3. Receive immediate HTTP response with `result: \"processing\"`.\n4. Monitor WebSocket for progress events.\n5. Receive final result via WebSocket.\n\nSet `response_mode` to `direct` to wait for a synchronous HTTP response instead of using WebSocket.\n\n**WebSocket Message Types:**\n- **Progress**: `{\"type\":\"progress\",\"step\":\"translation|ai_processing|anonymization|medical_question|finalizing\",\"message\":\"...\",\"percentage\":10-95}`\n- **Result**: `{\"type\":\"result\",\"status\":\"success\",\"data\":{...}}` (same payload shape as HTTP final response)\n- **Error**: `{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"...\",\"code\":\"...\"}`\n\n**Response:** A successful educational answer includes:\n- **`medicalAnswer`**: concise educational text in the same language as the question\n- **`data`**: empty array (Ask does not return a differential list)\n- language detection, anonymization metadata, and intent-routing fields (`queryType`, `intentAction`, `intentReason`, optional `suggestedPage`)\n\nThe answer does not diagnose the user. When the question describes symptoms, relevant urgent warning signs are included in the educational response.\n\n**Supported Languages**: The question can be in any language supported by Azure AI Translator (see [supported languages](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/translator/language-support)). The response will be returned in the same language as the input. If the optional parameter `lang` is not provided, the language is detected automatically.\n\n**Anonymization**: The response includes anonymized versions of the submitted text where personally identifiable information (PII) is replaced with [ANON-N] (where N is the character count), and then converted to asterisks in the final output. PII includes full names, addresses, contact details, Social Security Numbers, and any unique identification numbers. Age is NOT considered PII and is preserved.\n\n**Queue System**: Requests may be queued during high traffic for any model. A queue status will be returned for tracking, including the selected processing region based on user timezone and model capacity.\n",
